"Why Blockchain Instead of a Database?"

A traditional database is typically controlled by a single organisation, 
and records can be modified by administrators. In contrast, blockchain stores transactions
across a distributed network where records are immutable and transparent. Smart contracts also allow business
rules to be executed automatically without requiring a trusted third party. For hotel bookings, this improves trust
, accountability and transparency between guests and hotel operators (Ethereum Foundation, 2024)
